{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core fluent api ef core fluent api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","fileName":"EF Core Fluent API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Fluent API","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]] [[ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core fluent api ef core fluent api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","fileName":"EF Core Fluent API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Fluent API","heading":"EF Core Fluent API","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The EF Core Fluent API configures a model through chained method calls, commonly in `OnModelCreating`. It can define keys, property constraints, relationships, indexes, table mappings, value generation, and behavior that conventions do not capture.\n\nFluent configuration keeps persistence details out of entity classes and can express mappings unavailable through attributes. When conventions, annotations, and Fluent API configuration conflict, the explicit Fluent configuration has the greatest authority.\n\nIn the book's service architecture, fluent configuration is part of the data-access layer and defines the database-facing model without moving those details into the HTTP or application-service layers.\n\nThis source uses `OnModelCreating` to complete mappings that conventions or annotations do not express cleanly, keeping database-oriented relationship and key configuration within the data-layer composition boundary.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core fluent api ef core fluent api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","fileName":"EF Core Fluent API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Fluent API","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n[[hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}